global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 385, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Financial performance for the 160-year-old insurance holding company mostly held steady in 2020: Revenue inched up 1.3% for the year, and net income\u2014at just shy of $2.7 billion\u2014rose 2.9%. But that was enough to move Travelers up eight spots on the Fortune 500. The company extended its Stay-at-Home Auto Premium Credit Program last year, giving its U.S. personal auto insurance customers a 15% credit on premiums in April, May, and June. The company also accelerated commission payments to eligible agents and brokers, assisting them by putting more cash in their pockets during a difficult time.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri, Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\" data-sheets-textstyleruns=\"{&quot;1&quot;:0}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:248,&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;6&quot;:1}}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:255}\">Financial performance for the 160-year-old insurance holding company mostly held steady in 2020: Revenue inched up 1.3% for the year, and net income\u2014at just shy of $2.7 billion\u2014rose 2.9%. But that was enough to move Travelers up 14 spots on the Global 500. The company extended its Stay-at-Home Auto Premium Credit Program last year, giving its U.S. personal auto insurance customers a 15% credit on premiums in April, May, and June. The company also accelerated commission payments to eligible agents and brokers, assisting them by putting more cash in their pockets during a difficult time.</span>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 98, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;Financial performance for the 160-year-old insurance holding company mostly held steady in 2020: Revenue inched up 1.3% for the year, and net income\u2014at just shy of $2.7 billion\u2014rose 2.9%. But that was enough to move Travelers up eight spots on the Fortune 500. The company extended its Stay-at-Home Auto Premium Credit Program last year, giving its U.S. personal auto insurance customers a 15% credit on premiums in April, May, and June. The company also accelerated commission payments to eligible agents and brokers, assisting them by putting more cash in their pockets during a difficult time.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri, Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\" data-sheets-textstyleruns=\"{&quot;1&quot;:0}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:248,&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;6&quot;:1}}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:255}\">Financial performance for the 160-year-old insurance holding company mostly held steady in 2020: Revenue inched up 1.3% for the year, and net income\u2014at just shy of $2.7 billion\u2014rose 2.9%. But that was enough to move Travelers up eight spots on the Fortune 500. The company extended its Stay-at-Home Auto Premium Credit Program last year, giving its U.S. personal auto insurance customers a 15% credit on premiums in April, May, and June. The company also accelerated commission payments to eligible agents and brokers, assisting them by putting more cash in their pockets during a difficult time.</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 399, "itemDescription": "The insurance holding company, which has been around more than 160 years, provides a wide range of commercial and personal property and casualty insurance products. The company's revenues have been impacted by COVID-19, but it says those loses have been somewhat mitigated by decreases in auto and other types of claims."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 202